==History==
2016
*The Clone [[Cards|card]] was added to the game on 9/12/2016.
2017
*On 13/3/2017, the [[Version History#March 2017 Update (13/3/2017)|March 2017 Update]] made it so that the would no longer reset charge attacks of [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]]. While it will no longer reset charge attacks of the original troops, the clones spawn without being charged, retaining its behavior prior to this change.
*On 12/6/2017, the [[Version History#June 2017 Update (12/6/2017)|June 2017 Update]] decreased the cloning time to 0.5 seconds (from 0.8 seconds).
2018
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]] allowed the Clone to be placed on the river.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]] increased the Clone's area radius to 4 tiles (from 3 tiles). It also moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Clone from Frozen Peak to Electro Valley.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]] changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8).
*On 1/10/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (1/10/2018)|Balance Update]] fixed a bug where troops that were spawned after their parent troops died could not be cloned.
2019
*On 28/1/2019, the [[Version History#January%202019%20Update%20(28/1/2019)|January 2019 Update]] made the cloned troops spawn behind the original troops instead of to the right.
*On 15/4/2019, the [[Version History#April%202019%20Update%20(15/4/2019)|April 2019 Update]] decreased the Clone's area radius to 3 tiles (from 4 tiles).
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]] removed the Clone from all [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Draft]] selections.
2020
*On 31/8/2020, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20II%20Update%20(31/8/2020)|Clan Wars II Update]] made it so that cloned troops can no longer be healed.
*On 10/9/2020, an [[Version History#Optional Update (10/9/2020)|Optional Update]] made it so that a cloned [[Skeleton Barrel]] would now function correctly.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]] moved the Arena to unlock the Clone from Electro Valley to Legendary Arena.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]] increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13). It also fixed unintended interaction with [[Goblin Drill]] and Clone.
*On 1/11/2021, an [[Version History#Optional%20Update%20(1/11/2021)|Optional Update]] fixed a bug where cloned troops that spawn troops after their parent troops died spawned non-cloned troops.
2022
*On 30/3/2022, the [[Version History#Miner%20Update%20(30/3/2022)|Miner Update]] added a card render to the Clone's card info screen.
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]] moved the Arena to unlock the Clone from Legendary Arena to Miner's Mine.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]] increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
*On 13/11/2023, a [[Version History#Minor%20Update%20(13/11/2023)|Minor Update]] fixed some bugs such as using Clone during the spawn timer pushed a troop forward, spawning two Guardiennes when at the right moment [[Little Prince]] used Royal Rescue, and [[Goblin Giant]] spawning spooky, floating, and bodyless [[Spear Goblins]].
2025
*On 1/4/2025, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (1/4/2025)|maintenance break]] fixed a bug where Clone's card info page did not display the correct card levels.

