==Trivia==
*The word "''Clone''" comes from the Greek "''klonos''", meaning branch.
*The Clone is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Heal]], [[Lightning]], [[Freeze]], [[Poison]], and [[Rage]].
**In Clash of Clans, the container for Clone resemble spells that take up 2 housing space (although the Clone takes up 3 housing space), whereas in Clash Royale, the container for the Clone resemble spells that take up only 1 housing space.
**Unlike its [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Clone_Spell Clash of Clans counterpart], the Clone only produces one clone of a [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] regardless of its size with an indefinite lifespan while in Clash of Clans, a single troop may produce multiple clones that are just as strong as the original, but is limited by a certain amount of housing space and they despawn after some time.
*In the French, Italian, and Arabic language settings of the game, the Clone's name translates to "Cloning". In the German and Chinese language settings of the game, the Clone's name translates to "Clone Spell". In the Korean, Persian, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Clone's name translates to "Cloning Magic", "Simulation", and "Replication" respectively.
*The Clone is 1 of 7 spells which have team-colored rings on their radius, the others are Earthquake, Freeze, Poison, Rage, [[Tornado]], and [[Graveyard]].
*A [[Barbarians|Barbarian]] is featured on the Clone's card render.
*The upgrades work like that of a [[Mirror]]. When leveling up the Clone, the cloned cards' Level will be increased. Along with the Mirror, Clone is the only card, which has a stat that does not increase at all levels. In its case, it is the Cloned {{Rarity|Legendary}} Level and Cloned {{Rarity|Champion}} Level stats.
*The Clone has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
** The Clone is 1 of 3 spells that has been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being [[Giant Snowball]] and [[Royal Delivery]].
** The Clone is 1 of 3 spells that has been featured in the Boost Fields game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Heal and Rage.
** The Clone is 1 of 5 spells that have been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Spell%20Cauldron|Spell Cauldron]] sub-mode of the [[Treasure Hunt]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Heal, Lightning, Freeze, and Rage.
*The Clone is unavailable in multiple special game modes. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 2 cards that is unavailable in Draft, the other being Mirror.
**It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in Mirror [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|mode]], the others being [[Minions]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Tesla]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Inferno Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], Freeze, [[X-Bow]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Monk]].
**It is 1 of 4 cards that is unavailable in Triple Draft, the others being [[Three Musketeers]], Giant Skeleton, and Mirror.
**It is 1 of 2 cards that is unavailable in Mega Draft, the other being Mirror.
**It is 1 of 3 cards that cannot be set on Defense Towers in [[Clan Wars]], the others being Elixir Collector and Mirror.
*The Clone creates a "popping" sound when casted. However, due to a glitch, if an opposing Clone is placed, no sound is played.
*Clone is the only spell that cannot affect [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]]. However, you can have a cloned building via a [[Cannon Cart]].
*Troops that fall from the sky when spawning do not fall from the sky when cloned.
*A cloned [[Star Points|Star Leveled]] unit will have the golden level number and skin.
*The [[Card Mastery]] task "Magnificent, Aren't They?" is a reference to a quote mentioned in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wars:_Episode_II_%E2%80%93_Attack_of_the_Clones Star Wars Attack of the Clones,] when [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obi-Wan_Kenobi Obi-Wan Kenobi] was inspecting the mysterious clone army.
*Before the Clone's card release, the Clone was made able to allow cloned troops to spawn troops after death.

